1
00:04:13,636 --> 00:04:19,636
This time he's fighting for his life.

2
00:08:27,272 --> 00:08:33,272
First Blood is a action, adventure, thriller film directed by Ted Kotcheff.

3
00:12:40,909 --> 00:12:46,909
When former Green Beret John Rambo is harassed by local law enforcement and arrested for vagrancy, he is
forced to flee into the mountains and wage an escalating one-man war against his pursuers.

4
00:16:54,545 --> 00:17:00,545
John Rambo, played by Sylvester Stallone.

5
00:21:08,181 --> 00:21:14,181
Col. Samuel Trautman, played by Richard Crenna.

6
00:25:21,818 --> 00:25:27,818
Hope Sheriff Will Teasle, played by Brian Dennehy.

7
00:29:35,454 --> 00:29:41,454
State Police Capt. Dave Kern, played by Bill McKinney.

8
00:33:49,090 --> 00:33:55,090
Deputy Sgt. Arthur Galt, played by Jack Starrett.

9
00:38:02,727 --> 00:38:08,727
Deputy Balford, played by Michael Talbott.

10
00:42:16,363 --> 00:42:22,363
First Blood is a 1982 American war action film starring
Sylvester Stallone as Vietnam War veteran John Rambo.

11
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
The film was directed by Ted Kotcheff and cowritten by Michael Kozoll, William
Sackheim and Stallone based on the 1972 novel First Blood by David Morrell.

12
00:50:43,636 --> 00:50:49,636
The story follows Rambo who, after entering a small town and clashing with the police,
attempts to survive a manhunt using his expertise in survival and combat skills.

13
00:54:57,272 --> 00:55:03,272
The film costars Richard Crenna as Rambo's mentor Colonel Sam
Trautman and Brian Dennehy as Sheriff Will Teasle.

14
00:59:10,909 --> 00:59:16,909
First Blood was released in the United States on October 22, 1982.

15
01:03:24,545 --> 01:03:30,545
Initial reviews were mixed, but the film was a box-office success, grossing $125.2 million and becoming the
13th-highest-grossing film at the domestic box office for the year and the seventh-highest-grossing film worldwide.

16
01:07:38,181 --> 01:07:44,181
In 1985, it also became the first Hollywood blockbuster to be released in China, holding the
record for the largest number of tickets sold for an American film until 2018.

17
01:11:51,818 --> 01:11:57,818
Since its release, it has been reappraised by critics, with many highlighting the roles of Stallone,
Dennehy and Crenna, and recognizing it as an influential film in the action genre.

18
01:16:05,454 --> 01:16:11,454
The film's success spawned the Rambo franchise, consisting of four sequels (cowritten by and starring
Stallone), an animated television series, a comic books series, a novel series and several video games.

19
01:20:19,090 --> 01:20:25,090
It was followed by Rambo: First Blood Part II, released in 1985.

20
01:24:32,727 --> 01:24:38,727
The film explores themes of prison, guerrilla warfare,
dying and death, vietnam war, vietnam veteran.

21
01:28:46,363 --> 01:28:52,363
The tone is dark and intense.
